      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is the piyyut “Aɐpid Nézer Ayom” by Elazar ben Qalir with the English translation of Paltiel Birnbaum found in his <tei:hi rend="italic">Maḥzor haShalem l’Rosh Hashanah v’Yom Kippur</tei:hi> (1951), pp. 223-226. There, Birnbaum offers the following commentary:</tei:p>
        <tei:p>אאפיד מזר, by Rabbi Elazar ha-Kallir, contains a double alphabetical acrostic, that is, the first word and the third word in each line begin with the same letter, like אאפיד-איום and בשלוש-ביום. The letters ה כ ס פ ר appear three times in their respective lines.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65983_notes"/>
